<div class="py-16 bg-[#FAF6EE]">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
    
    <div class="text-center space-y-3">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#9E472A] uppercase tracking-widest">Heritage & Culture</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-[#140B07]">The Ethiopian Buna Ceremony</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 max-w-xl mx-auto">
        A guide to the time-honored spiritual and social ritual of brewing coffee using the traditional Jebena pot, Frankincense, and Ketema grass.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step by Step Ritual Guide -->
    <div class="space-y-8 bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-[#EFE7DA] shadow-sm">
      
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <div class="flex items-start space-x-6 border-b border-[#EFE7DA] pb-8">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-[#24130D] text-[#E5A652] font-serif font-bold text-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">1</div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-[#140B07]">Preparing the Spatial Sanctuary</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            The floor is strewn with fresh green grass or braided <strong>Ketema mats (ቄጠማ)</strong>, bringing the vital energy of nature indoors. An embroidered <strong>Tibeb runner (ጥበብ)</strong> is draped across the wooden <strong>Rekebot serving table</strong>. A brazier (Fernello) is lit with charcoal, upon which <strong>Tigray Frankincense (ዕጣን)</strong> is cast to perfume the room.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <div class="flex items-start space-x-6 border-b border-[#EFE7DA] pb-8">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-[#24130D] text-[#E5A652] font-serif font-bold text-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">2</div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-[#140B07]">Roasting in the Menkeshkesh (መንከሽከሽ)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            Raw washed or natural green beans (Sidamo or Yirgacheffe) are washed clean, then roasted over hot coals in a perforated iron pan called the <strong>Menkeshkesh</strong>. When the beans release their dark oils and aromatic smoke, the pan is carried among guests so they may cup the smoke with their hands and inhale the fragrant bounty.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <div class="flex items-start space-x-6 border-b border-[#EFE7DA] pb-8">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-[#24130D] text-[#E5A652] font-serif font-bold text-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">3</div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-[#140B07]">Pounding & Fine Milling</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            The roasted beans are ground finely using a heavy wooden mortar and pestle (Mukecha and Zenezena) or a precision fine mill. The grounds are brought to a powdery flour consistency to allow complete emulsion in the hot water.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <div class="flex items-start space-x-6">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-[#24130D] text-[#E5A652] font-serif font-bold text-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">4</div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-[#140B07]">Brewing in the Clay Jebena (ጀበና)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            The coffee grounds and fresh spring water are poured into the spherical belly of the clay Jebena pot and placed on the coals. As the liquid reaches a boil, it rises through the neck and is decanted into a cooling cup, then returned to the Jebena several times. The brew is poured in a continuous, unbroken arch into small ceramic <strong>Sini cups (ሲኒ)</strong>, served with roasted barley snack (Kolo) and fresh rue herb (Tenadam).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Sourcing & Kenyan Dispatch Info -->
    <div class="bg-[#24130D] text-white p-8 rounded-3xl border border-[#9E472A]/40 space-y-4">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-[#E5A652]">Bringing the Tradition to Kenya</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        Yebente Buna bridges the ancient coffee traditions of Ethiopia with Kenya's discerning coffee lovers. All orders are packed in Addis Ababa, transported through the Moyale Border Post under verified customs, and dispatched to your Kenyan residence via Fargo Courier or Sendy.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <%= link_to "Explore All Products & Sourcing", products_path, class: "inline-flex px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-[#00A859] text-white font-semibold text-xs hover:bg-[#008F4C] transition-all" %>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
